QuestGuidance.Register("en",459,{
[14657]="7004956C\n1\tEnter the ruins of Barad-dûr\tBarad-dûr can be found to the south-east of Lûghash in Dor Amarth. King Váskmun Greytooth of the Stout-axes can be found somewhere deep within the dungeons of Barad-dûr. You should begin your search in the ruins of the Dark Tower.\n2\tSearch for the dungeons within the ruins of Barad-dûr\tBarad-dûr can be found to the south-east of Lûghash in Dor Amarth. You have entered Barad-dûr and should now seek the dungeons in the depths of the Dark Tower.\n3\tFind King Váskmun Greytooth in the depths of Barad-dûr\tKing Váskmun Greytooth can be found deep within the dungeons of Barad-dûr. You have found imprisoned Stout-axes, but you still have no found King Greytooth. You should proceed deeper into the dungeons of Barad-dûr and continue your search.\n4\tTalk to King Váskmun Greytooth\tKing Váskmun Greytooth can be found in his cell in the dungeons of Barad-dûr. You have found the King of the Stout-axes at a curious moment. It appears he has overpowered his captors, and now means to escape. You should speak to him on behalf of Spakorth.\n5\tFind King Váskmun Greytooth's armour in the dungeon armoury of Barad-dûr\030Find King Váskmun Greytooth some food at the larder in Barad-dûr\030Find King Váskmun Greytooth's lockbox in Sauron's relic-chamber\tKing Váskmun Greytooth's armour can be found among the collected weapons at the armoury, rations of some kind can be found in the larder within the dungeons of Barad-dûr, and his mithril lockbox can be found in a small chamber near the main gate of Barad-dûr. King Váskmun Greytooth has asked for you to aid in his escape by finding him some food, his old armour, and a mithril lockbox that was taken from him by Sauron.\n6\tDeliver the equipment to King Váskmun Greytooth in Barad-dûr\tKing Váskmun Greytooth can be found in his cell in the dungeons of Barad-dûr. You have found King Greytooth some food as well as his ornate, golden armour, but you were unable to find his lockbox. You should deliver his equipment to him in his cell in Barad-dûr.\n7\tTalk to King Váskmun Greytooth in Lûghash\tKing Váskmun Greytooth can be found on the central level of Lûghash. You have returned to Lûghash with King Váskmun Greytooth and should now speak to him before he addresses his folk.\n",
[14658]="70054FED\n1\tFind the 'wall of shadow' in Falch Gurth\tThe 'wall of shadow' can be found to the south of Torgris in Falch Gurth. Cuilion has asked you to enter Falch Gurth and learn what has become of the company of Rangers who sought to explore Thuringwath.\n2\tTalk to Mithrandir\tMithrandir can be found in Falch Gurth. You have discovered the 'wall of shadow' of which Taurdir spoke, but it appears Mithrandir followed in your wake. You should talk to him.\n3\tCast a stone into the shadows of Falch Gurth\tA stone can be found in Falch Gurth. Mithrandir has asked you to cast a stone into the shadows of Falch Gurth. You should pick up a nearby stone and cast it into the darkness.\n4\tTalk to Mithrandir\tMithrandir can be found within Falch Gurth. After casting a stone into the shadows of Thuringwath, it appears to be gone from the world. You should talk to Mithrandir.\n",
[14659]="70057D28\n1\tDeliver strawberry buns to Melthend (total: 6)\tThe crafting recipe for the strawberry buns can be bartered for from the marriage-wright, Melthend. Strawberry bun kits can be earned by completing Midsummer quests in Hobbiton-Bywater and at the Party Tree.\n",
[14660]="70057D29\n1\tDeliver wedding centrepieces to Melthend (total: 3)\tThe crafting recipe for the wedding centrepieces can be bartered for from the marriage-wright, Melthend. Wedding centrepiece kits can be earned by completing Midsummer quests in Duillond.\n",
[14661]="70057D26\n1\tDeliver banners of the newly-wed to Melthend (total: 3)\tThe crafting recipe for the banners of the newly-wed can be bartered for from the marriage-wright, Melthend. Banner of the newly-wed kits can be earned by completing Midsummer quests in Bree-town.\n",
[14662]="70057D27\n1\tDeliver midsummer drinking horns to Melthend (total: 3)\tThe crafting recipe for a midsummer drinking horn can be bartered for from the marriage-wright, Melthend. Drinking horn kits can be found by completing Midsummer quests in Thorin's Hall.\n",
[14663]="7004E4EE\n1\tDefeat Jangovar (total: 15)\tThe Jangovar are attacking Hammerstead! You should defeat the Jangovar forces.\n2\tTalk to Lóssi\tYou should talk to Lóssi, who can be found defending Hammerstead.\n",
[14664]="70034683\n1\tThe refugees are huddled in their tiny camp south-west of Dunfast. You should ask the refugees if they observed any relic to cause the ice-spire to appear where Núrzum sat.\t\n2\tTell Cyneberg of the survivors' plight\tCyneberg is at the refugee's hideout south-west of Dunfast. You should speak with Cyneberg.\n",
[14665]="7004E8DF\n1\tSearch for the wizard in the woods\tYou should search the Thornholt woods, south of Skarháld, for the odd wizard Stráhek the Stout encountered.\n2\tTalk to Radagast\tThe wizard stands among the wood of Thornholt, south of Skarháld. You should talk to the not so odd, actually familiar wizard in the woods.\n",
[14666]="70059745\n1\tPick up the summoning horn\tThe road to Old Man Willow has taken you deep into the Old Forest. You should pick up the summoning horn to call Marigold to your side.\n2\tDefeat Gulmúk Dampmould\tThe wood-trolls are corrupting the forest. You should defeat their leader, Gulmúk Dampmould.\n3\tDestroy the sword\tThough the wood-trolls have lost their leader, fell spirits continue to flock to the Old Forest. You should destroy the sword that has been summoning the spirits.\n",
[14667]="70059744\n1\tDefeat Gulmúk Dampmould\tThe wood-trolls are corrupting the forest. You should defeat their leader, Gulmúk Dampmould.\n2\tDestroy the sword\tThough the wood-trolls have lost their leader, fell spirits continue to flock to the Old Forest. You should destroy the sword that has been summoning the spirits.\n",
[14668]="70059743\n1\tDefeat Gulmúk Dampmould\tThe wood-trolls are corrupting the forest. You should defeat their leader, Gulmúk Dampmould.\n2\tDestroy the sword\tThough the wood-trolls have lost their leader, fell spirits continue to flock to the Old Forest. You should destroy the sword that has been summoning the spirits.\n",
[14669]="70059742\n1\tDefeat Gulmúk Dampmould\tThe wood-trolls are corrupting the forest. You should defeat their leader, Gulmúk Dampmould.\n2\tDestroy the sword\tThough the wood-trolls have lost their leader, fell spirits continue to flock to the Old Forest. You should destroy the sword that has been summoning the spirits.\n",
[14670]="70066CC9\n1\tTalk to Luingil in Echad Lendir\tSiliveth has asked you to check on their companion Luingil. Luingil can be found in Echad Lendir.\n",
[14671]="7002E526\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Oseg\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (quantity: see journal)\tThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.\n",
[14672]="7002E533\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Oseg\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (quantity: see journal)\tThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.\n",
[14673]="7002E52F\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Oseg\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (quantity: see journal)\tThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.\n",
[14674]="7002E525\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Oseg\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (quantity: see journal)\tThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.\n",
[14675]="70015E4C\n1\tDefeat wolves (total: 16)\tWolves can be found throughout Eregion. Golgallon has asked that you search out and destroy the wolves that plague Eregion.\n2\tTalk to Golgallon at Echad Eregion\tGolgallon is in Echad Eregion. You should return to Golgallon and inform him of your success against the wolves.\n",
[14676]="7002618C\n1\tDefeat Gauredain at the Even-rills (total: 8)\tThe Even-rills are north-east of the Eavespires. Lithuifin asked you to head to the Even-rills and defeat the Gauredain there.\n2\tTalk to Lithuifin at the Eavespires\tLithuifin is at the Eavespires, south-west of the Even-rills. Lithuifin will want to hear the Guaredain have been driven out of the Even-rills.\n",
[14677]="7000758C\n1\tBring the wolf-pelts to Roger Hawkling\030Collect wolf-pelts (total: 5)\tThere are wolves in the Old Forest. Roger Hawkling has asked you to help repel the threat of wolves in the area, bringing him their pelts as evidence of your work.\n",
[14678]="70062141\n1\tRetrieve Hal's stolen bow\tHal Wolfscomb has asked you to retrieve his bow, which was stolen by Orcs. The Orc who stole Hal's bow is at Tharbad, in Cardolan.\n2\tReturn to Hal\tYou should bring the stolen bow back to Hal Wolfscomb. Hal is at camp in northern Tharbad in Cardolan.\n",
[14679]="700032BF\n1\tDefeat wolves at wolf den (total: 8)\tThe wolf den is off the road north of Dora Brownlock's farm and Waymeet. Dora Brownlock is grateful that you rescued her chickens from the wolves, but she is afraid to go home until she is sure that the wolves will no longer trouble her. She has asked you to go to the wolf den and put an end to the threat.\n2\tTalk to Dora Brownlock\tDora Brownlock is at the centre of Waymeet. Dora Brownlock will be pleased to hear that you have done something about the wolves threatening the area.\n",
[14680]="7003EB00\n1\tDefeat Gauredain in Tâl Bruinen (total: 10)\tGauredain are encamped at Echad Gauradan in Tâl Bruinen, in the Trollshaws. While in Tâl Bruinen, you should defeat the Gauredain who have encamped there.\n",
[14681]="700087FF\n1\tDefeat Darktide-wolves (total: 10)\tWolves can be found east and west of Hoarhallow, scattered throughout Hithlad and into the hills of the Steps of Gram. Emerald Twospade explained that the wolves of the Ettenmoors have long been the true threat against the Little Folk of Hoarhallow. She enlisted your aid in destroying the creatures and lessening their threat.\n2\tReturn to Emerald Twospade at Hoarhallow\tEmerald Twospade is in Hoarhallow. You scoured through the Grimwood and slew a large number of the Darktide-wolves. You should return to Emerald Twospade with the news.\n",
[14682]="7003E4B1\n1\tFind Pothlorn\tPothlorn was scouting the path which leads north and east through the Gorges to Ost Thondol. Elladan asked you to search for the missing Elf-scout, Pothlorn, and learn whether or not he still lives.\n",
[14683]="7000E373\n1\tDefeat wolves (total: 14)\tWolves can be found across much of Taur Orthon. Urho has asked you to help him by hunting the wolves which destroyed his tent.\n2\tTalk to Urho\tUrho is on the north-west road, next to his ruined guard-post. You have slain many wolves and should now report to Urho with news of your success.\n",
[14684]="70066662\n1\tDefeat wolves in Eryn Asgath (0/12)\tWolves can be found in Eryn Asgath near Tarlang's Neck in the Blackroot Vale.\n2\tDefeat wolves in Eryn Asgath (total: 12)\tWolves can be found in Eryn Asgath near Tarlang's Neck in the Blackroot Vale. You have discovered the den of the wolves that recently invaded the Blackroot Vale. You should defeat them and make safe the road through Tarlang's Neck.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated a number of wolves at Eryn Asgath.\n",
[14685]="70000D9D\n1\tDefeat wolves in Puddifoot's Fields (total: 6)\tThere are wolves in Cam Puddifoot's fields to the east of Budgeford. Hyacinth Took sent you to Cam Puddifoot to request delivery of some saltpetre for Lobelia Sackville-Baggins' fireworks. Farmer Puddifoot is willing to deliver the saltpetre, but he wants you to clear his fields of wolves first.\n2\tTalk to Cam Puddifoot\tCam Puddifoot is near his home in Budgeford. Cam Puddifoot is willing to send saltpetre to Hyacinth Took, but first he requested your help clearing wolves from his fields. With the threat of wolves lessened, you should return to him.\n3\tBring the saltpetre to Hyacinth Took\tHyacinth Took is near the Great Smials in Tuckborough. While you were helping to clear the wolves from Cam Puddifoot's fields, the pig-farmer collected a pack of saltpetre for you to take back to Hyacinth Took.\n",
[14686]="7006609B\n1\tDefeat vale-wolves (total: 8)\tDornach has asked you to thin the number of wolves sharing the forest with his people. Defeat vale-wolves around the lumber camp east of Ethring.\n2\tTalk to Dornach\tYou have defeated many wolves, and should report back to Dornach. Talk to Dornach at the lumber camp east of Ethring.\n",
[14687]="700372D4\n1\tDefeat wolves and Warg-riders east of Stoke (total: 10)\tWarg-riders and wolves haunt the fields to the east of Stoke. Dudsig has asked you to deal with the threat of Warg-riders and wolves which plague the people of the Broadacres.\n2\tTalk to Dudsig\tDudsig is at the Oserley encampment outside the north-east gate of Stoke. You should return to Stoke and tell Dudsig of your victories.\n",
[14688]="7001931A\n1\tDefeat wolves in Nen Hilith (total: 6)\tWolves can be found in Nen Hilith, south-west of the Elf-camp. Helhathel has asked you to defeat wolves in Nen Hilith in order to restore balance in the valley.\n2\tTalk to Helhathel in Nen Hilith\tHelhathel at the Elf-camp, north-west of the wolf-haunts. You successfully defeated a number of wolves within the valley of Nen Hilith and should return to Helhathel with your report.\n",
})
